{"name":"Humble Hippo","hex":"#aaaa99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"humble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not pretentious or magnificent; unpretending; unassuming.","Having a low position or a low opinion of oneself; not proud, arrogant, or assuming; modest."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["People with a low position or a low opinion of themselves; those who are not proud, arrogant, or assuming.","An arrest based on weak evidence intended to demean or punish the subject."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humble"},{"term":"hippo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of hippopotamus.","An armored personnel carrier used by the South African Defence Force."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hippo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hippopotamus","blocks":[{"text":"The hippopotamus, often shortened to hippo, further qualified as the common hippopotamus, Nile hippopotamus and river hippopotamus, is a large semiaquatic mammal native to sub-Saharan Africa. It is one of only two extant species in the family Hippopotamidae, the other being the pygmy hippopotamus. Its name comes from the Ancient Greek for \"river horse\" (ἱπποπόταμος)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Portrait_Hippopotamus_in_the_water.jpg/330px-Portrait_Hippopotamus_in_the_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippopotamus","wikidata":"Q34505"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Hippopotamus_distribution.png/500px-Hippopotamus_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Hippopotamus_distribution.png/500px-Hippopotamus_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A